+Ansible facts are data related to your remote systems, including operating systems, IP addresses, attached filesystems, and more. You can access this data in the ``ansible_facts`` variable. By default, you can also access some Ansible facts as top-level variables with the ``ansible_`` prefix. You can disable this behavior using the :ref:`INJECT_FACTS_AS_VARS` setting.
+
+On Linux, ``ansible_facts.locally_reachable_ips`` contains ``ipv4`` and ``ipv6`` lists of locally reachable addresses and prefixes from local routes. The lists are normalized, de-duplicated, and ordered by address. For example, use ``ansible_facts.locally_reachable_ips.ipv4`` to access IPv4 ranges.
+
+To see all available facts, add this task to a play:
 
 .. code-block:: yaml
 
